Senior Partner Growth Manager &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are Ocado Commercial,&lt;/strong&gt; and we are revolutionising online grocery. We partner with the world&#39;s leading retailers, providing our innovative Ocado Smart Platform (OSP) – a powerful blend of automation and software – to elevate their e-commerce capabilities. Join us and be part of a team that&#39;s shaping the future of retail, working with global giants from Kroger to AEON.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Partner Growth Manager role is an exciting opportunity in our Partner Success Team to directly influence the commercial success of our partners, some of the largest retailers in EMEA. This position will require reasonable travel to Saudi Arabia and/or Europe.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Businesses that partner with Ocado come in all shapes and sizes, and leverage our technology in different ways.&amp;nbsp; In this role, you will combine your knowledge of ecommerce, grocery retail, and online marketing with communication skills and analytical abilities to shape and influence how our partners grow online.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Partner Growth Manager will work with the Ocado Partner Account team to drive the growth agenda in our partner’s business, enabling our partners to improve commercial outcomes, grow their customer base, order volume, and overall profitability.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build effective relationships with key commercial, marketing, and ecommerce stakeholders in our partners’ businesses. You will leverage knowledge of customer objectives, strategic know-how, knowledge of the Ocado Smart Platform (OSP), as well as the expertise of our central growth subject matter experts to create and implement successful growth strategies. You will become a first line of e-commerce growth support, leveraging our team of central subject matter experts for more in-depth support. You will support your internal stakeholders in the region with insights and reporting on growth topics, as well as be a source of information and support for your partners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the Partner Success Team you will be responsible for&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;supporting our partners in their day to day use of OSP, ensuring that their webshop is configured optimally, using the most impactful OSP features, to drive maximum customer acquisition, retention and basket size.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will consult with partners through both in-depth projects in close collaboration with our Central Growth and/or Technology teams, as well as ongoing optimisation forums aimed at improving their commercial performance. You will leverage data to drive recommendations that improve overall performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Partner Growth Manager is accountable for shaping and delivering growth strategy for their assigned Partner(s), supporting improved commercial outcomes including customer acquisition, retention, order growth and profitability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works closely with the Partner’s ecommerce, marketing and technology teams and cross-functional Ocado stakeholders to align growth priorities and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uses growth, trading and customer data and analytics to understand commercial performance, identify trends and opportunities, and deliver clear, actionable recommendations to Partners and internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accountable for translating Partner growth objectives into clear, prioritised growth initiatives and optimisation opportunities that support long-term commercial success, maximising the potential of the OSP platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acts as Ocado’s primary growth and ecommerce subject matter expert for the Partner, using deep knowledge of OSP capabilities and growth / go-to-market expertise to shape recommendations on ecommerce configuration, trading, monetisation and customer experience, as well as sustainable marketing and communications adapted to the local competitive landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owns the Partner relationship for e-commerce and growth OSP roadmap engagement, acting as the named point of contact for, trading, monetisation, customer experience roadmap topic, and, in general, any non-operational topic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represents Partner growth and ecommerce requirements and priorities into Ocado’s roadmap governance processes, supporting feature discovery with clear problem definition, context and Partner business case and value articulation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitors delivery and adoption of growth-critical features and capabilities, working with internal teams and Partners to maximise realised commercial value and improve utilisation of growth-enabling functionality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifies and escalates risks, dependencies or delivery issues that may impact the Partner’s ability to realise growth from OSP capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Languages: Fluency in English is essential. Arabic and European languages are highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bias to action, capable of designing data-driven strategies but also secure implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder, relationship building and networking skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A team player who’s comfortable interacting with Partner teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated with an ability to deliver to deadlines and multi-task under pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable dealing with ambiguity and uncertainty&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to handle difficult situations, facing challenges with positivity, confidence and pragmatism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in one or several of the following fields:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance marketing within a direct to consumer business (grocery ecommerce experience a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial or trading experience in a direct to consumer business ( grocery ecommerce experience a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retail management consulting&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity and passion for data-driven marketing, consumer insight, and ecommerce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with or experience with measuring and optimizing key growth metrics including user growth, conversion, LTV&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in supporting our people with meaningful, flexible benefits that prioritise well-being and work-life balance. Here’s a snapshot of what you can expect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time to recharge&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;25 days annual leave (rising to 27 after 5 years), plus the option to buy more – and 30 days a year to work from anywhere in the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health &amp;amp; wellbeing&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;Private Medical Insurance from your first month, wellbeing support through specialist apps and EAP, plus Income Protection and Life Assurance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Family-first policies&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;22 weeks paid maternity/primary carer leave and 6 weeks paid paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial support&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;Pension with employer matching up to 7%, share schemes (Sharesave &amp;amp; BAYE), and interest-free loans for train tickets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commuter perks&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;Cycle to Work Scheme and free shuttle buses to/from Hatfield and Welwyn Garden City stations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exclusive discounts&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;15% off at Ocado.com with free delivery (starting in your first month).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ocado Group is an equal opportunities employer and as such makes every effort to ensure that all potential employees are treated fairly and equally, regardless of their sex, sexual orientation, marital status, race, colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin, religion or belief, age, or disability or union membership status.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Commercial Europe (Department)  Hatfield

Senior Controlling Manager (Finance) &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Host Broadcast Services (HBS) is a leading, independent host broadcast specialist, dedicated to helping international sports federations, organising committees, and rights holders deliver their events to a global audience. We provide world-class broadcast solutions for some of the world’s biggest sporting events, including the prestigious FIFA World Cup™, ensuring broadcasters worldwide can offer fans a unique and engaging viewing experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Zug, Switzerland, and as part of the Infront Sports &amp;amp; Media group, HBS offers the full spectrum of host broadcast operations and services — combining technological innovation with deep industry expertise to set the benchmark in live sports broadcasting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🌍&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Senior Controlling Manager | Paris | 15-Month Contract | International Group Finance Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📍&lt;strong&gt; Paris, France | International Media &amp;amp; Sports Environment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💬&lt;strong&gt; Fluent in English and French.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📅 &lt;strong&gt;CDD - start early 2027 (15-Month Fixed-Term Contract with possible opportunities for extension)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you a senior finance professional looking for your next challenge in a dynamic, international business?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HBS is seeking an experienced Senior Controlling Manager to lead our international Controlling function on a 15-month fixed-term contract. Reporting to the Head of Finance, you will oversee a multi-country controlling team and play a key role in financial planning, reporting, project controlling, and strategic decision-making across our global operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading a Controlling team based across France, Switzerland, the UK and the USA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving financial performance reporting for projects, business units and international subsidiaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing budgeting, forecasting, cash flow forecasting and monthly management reporting&lt;br&gt;Supporting strategic planning and business growth initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering with senior stakeholders across Finance, Operations and Executive Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to process improvements and ERP development initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years&#39; experience in Financial Controlling within an international environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven leadership experience, ideally managing geographically dispersed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of IFRS and project-based financial management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical and business partnering skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieved Master Degree (or equivalent) in Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel capabilities; Business Central experience is an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English required; French is beneficial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an excellent opportunity for an experienced finance leader who enjoys working in a fast-paced, multicultural environment and wants to make an immediate impact within a globally recognised sports broadcast organisation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;HBS is committed to creating an inclusive and diverse workplace. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates and will provide reasonable adjustments to support candidates with disabilities or specific needs throughout the recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We thrive on delivering world-class broadcast solutions for major international events. We’re always looking for exceptional individuals who demonstrate:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Communication Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;– Fluent in English, able to navigate an international environment with clarity and professionalism.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Confident &amp;amp; Adaptable Team Players&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;– Thriving in fast-paced, live event settings, where collaboration is key to success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Excellence &amp;amp; Organisation&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;– Structured, detail-oriented, and proficient in the tools needed to keep operations seamless&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who is HBS?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ve probably watched a football game at some point in your life. Well, if it was a World Cup match, it was likely filmed and produced by the HBS (Host Broadcast Services) team. We are involved in the production of the following events: FIFA World Cup 26™, FIFA Women’s World Cup 2027™, Men’s Rugby World Cup 2027 Australia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Find out more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hbs.tv/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;www.hbs.tv&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to the high volume of applications, we may not be able to respond individually to every candidate, but we will do our best to get back to you regarding next steps. Thank you for your interest in joining HBS.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Finance and Administration  Boulogne-Billancourt

(Senior) Research Consultant DACH (B2B Focus) (m/f/d) &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Allow us to introduce ourselves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hello there! We’re Appinio, a global market research company that combines an AI-powered insights platform with expert consultancy. On a mission to make the world a little more fact-based, we help companies understand how consumers think and make smarter decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We started out in Hamburg back in 2014, but we’re now humbled to call the world our playground, with over &lt;strong&gt;260 employees&lt;/strong&gt; spread across &lt;strong&gt;13 countries &lt;/strong&gt;(we’re remote-first), 2600+ international clients, delivering research from &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;+190 markets,&lt;/strong&gt; globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Want to be a part of the Appinio movement? &lt;strong&gt;🚀&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-preserver-spaces=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Here at Appinio, we value &lt;strong&gt;transparency&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;in our recruitment process&lt;/strong&gt;, and we&#39;ve created a blog to share what to expect during each step of our journey together:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-preserver-spaces=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-preserver-spaces=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--focus-visible&quot; href=&quot;https://www.appinio.com/en/blog/life-at-appinio/appinio-recruitment-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.appinio.com/en/blog/life-at-appinio/appinio-recruitment-process&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mission as a (Senior) Research Consultant&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;(Senior)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Research Consultant (m/f/d) &lt;/strong&gt;with a strong quantitative market research background to join our newly dedicated B2B research team in the DACH region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This specialized unit focuses on research projects that specifically survey B2B target groups, professional decision-makers, and niche business audiences (rather than only standard B2C consumer panels). You will work closely with leading global strategy and management consultancies as well as major international corporates, supporting high-stakes projects where research needs to be delivered quickly, precisely, and with a clear focus on the business question.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;End-to-End B2B Project Lead: Manage quantitative research projects end-to-end, including B2B screening design, questionnaire drafting, platform setup, fieldwork monitoring, and data delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Methodology &amp;amp; Study Design: Optimise bespoke study designs across core use cases (e.g., Target Group Analysis, U&amp;amp;A, Pricing studies, Concept Testing) mainly tailored to hard-to-reach professional audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior Client Sparring &amp;amp; Advisory: Act as a trusted research partner to leading global consulting firms and major corporate clients. Work directly with experienced consultants and senior stakeholders to translate business questions into robust research approaches, advise on sample feasibility and survey methodology, and make pragmatic decisions when timelines are tight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial &amp;amp; Scoping Collaboration: Partner closely with Sales and Account Management on project scoping, feasibility checks, and methodology definition for complex project requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process &amp;amp; Quality Enhancement: Contribute to standardizing B2B screening protocols, sampling frameworks, and best practices to coach other researcher and safeguard delivery speed and research quality across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will thrive in this role if&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
